					</td>
					<td id="JoinCell" width="100%" valign="top"><P>Oryx is a guild comprised of raiders that aim to work with each other towards a common goal; to advance together as a cohesive unit. We are all not the best of friends here, but we get along as best as possible, and respect one another knowing the talents each of us have.<BR><BR>Joining Oryx is not a simple application, come on one raid, then get tagged. We like to keep our guild small in numbers, taking only what we absolutly need, and cherry picking the best we can get. If you do apply, please dont get discouraged if after 2 or 3 weeks you're still not tagged. The officers and myself like to make sure you would be the right fit with us, melding together with the rest of the guild, also assuring us that you can do your part and contribute like the rest of Oryx does on a nightly basis.<BR><BR>We raid as much as we can during the week. Raids start normally around 6pm CST, and end around 1-2 CST, depending on where and what we are aiming for. We have a channel, /oryx, that you are more then welcome to hang out in, see if help is needed, groups forming up or to see when the raid call is being made.<BR><BR>We're on no set faction, except our mages are pos CoV. If you need / want to keep your faction thats up to you, but, /q'ing out on every mob that has a negavite faction hit for you does get old, so please keep that in mind when you apply. Also keep in mind that 90% of the mobs we aim for have better rewards then you're aiming to quest for, so please do not let faction discourage you.<BR><BR>Loot. We have no RPP system, yet use a combination of default / closed roll system deteremined by the officers and I. Applicants can not roll against a guilded member for any item, period. Applicants may roll on items that are going to rot, or such items as quest armor from WTOV or NTOV, whichever place we might be that particular raid.<BR></P>
<P>- Solanthious</P><br></td>

